Subject: [PATCH] Replace an unbridged hotplug main device before attaching its successor

A wireless interface can move between radios before the previous device is
removed. Clearing its hotplug main device invalidates the cached master.
Refresh that pointer before testing for bridge operations, otherwise the old
non-bridge device rejects the replacement and leaves the interface unavailable.
Configured masters and removal of a different device retain their existing
ownership checks.

--- a/interface.c
+++ b/interface.c
@@ -1285,8 +1285,10 @@
 		return 0;
 	}
 
-	if (iface->main_dev.hotplug)
+	if (iface->main_dev.hotplug) {
 		interface_set_main_dev(iface, NULL);
+		mdev = iface->main_dev.dev;
+	}
 
 	if (mdev) {
 		if (mdev->hotplug_ops)
